---
title: Embedding operations
description: Put a live, interactive API operation inside a guide.
---

A guide that explains an endpoint can show the endpoint itself: its parameters, request body, responses, and a **Try** console. Embed one with the `api-operation` Markdoc tag:

```markdoc
{% api-operation spec="bookstore" path="/orders" method="post" title="Place an order" /%}
```

{% api-operation spec="bookstore" path="/orders" method="post" title="Place an order" /%}

## Attributes

| Attribute | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| `spec` | **Required.** The `id` of an API in `apis:`. |
| `path` | **Required.** The path as written in the spec, with its `{parameters}`. |
| `method` | `get` (default), `post`, `put`, `patch`, `delete`, ... |
| `title` | A heading for the embed. Default: the operation's summary. |
| `version` | One of the API's [versions](/docs/api-reference/versions/). Default: its default version. |

An unknown `spec` id shows a notice on the page and a build warning, so a typo doesn't go unnoticed.

## How it works

The embed is RapiDoc's `<rapi-doc-mini>` element showing one operation of the spec. It follows the portal theme and accent color.

Only pages with an embed load the RapiDoc bundle. Other docs pages stay light.

## Try from a guide

**Try** sends a real request to the spec's server. In this site's example spec, the server is the local mock: run `npm run mock` in the [RapiDocPortal repository](https://github.com/rapi-doc/RapiDocPortal) and the console above answers. See [Mock server](/docs/tools/mock-server/).

With sign-in and `auth.tryIt`, the embed fills in the signed-in reader's access token. See [Try with the reader's token](/docs/access/try-it/).

## In MDX or Markdown

The tag is Markdoc only. In an `.md` or `.mdx` guide, link to the operation on its reference page instead: `/apis/bookstore/orders#create-order`.
